{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ncur=[i for i in json.load(open('state.json'))['interpretations'] if i['id'].startswith('667e7866')][0]\nkn={k['id']:k for k in json.load(open('state.json'))['knowledge']}\nex=\\\"bd1e9e66ffbc4ab58902e32fdb7a0096\\\"\n\npara=(\\\"Restart in the grown direction, receipt %s (completed, tests_passed, exit 0): the leader's AddVoter for a new server failed at the store while the in-memory latest configuration grew to three voters at index 3 over a stored log that ended at 2; the leader then lost contact with the other committed voter, stayed leader through the phantom quorum, and committed a client command at index 4 while that committed voter's log ended at 2. Parsed index 0 records that sequence. Parsed index 1 records what the same node loaded after it was shut down and a fresh Raft was started over its own retained store: the configuration lists only A and B with two voters, the new server is absent, the last stored index is still 4 and the stored commit index reads 0. The phantom configuration is therefore confined to the process that installed it, and the entry that was committed under it survives as an ordinary stored entry whose commitment is no longer recorded, so its fate is decided afterwards by the committed pair rather than by the phantom configuration. Declared comparison: the request's single comparison did not correlate because the two events carry different case labels, phantom_commit and phantom_restart, so it was recorded as unknown; the events themselves are complete and are read directly here.\\\") % ex\n\nces=list(cur['counterevidence'])\nces[0]=ces[0].rstrip()+\\\" The grown direction now has the same measurement: in receipt %s the restarted node loaded only the committed pair and reported the new server absent, although the entry committed under the phantom quorum remained in its log at index 4.\\\" % ex\n\nlims=list(cur['limitations'])\nlims.append(\\\"Receipt %s restarts the leader once, immediately after the lone commit, with the committed peer still partitioned and no snapshot; it therefore does not show whether a later restart, or one after the entry reaches the committed peer, changes the loaded configuration, and it does not test a second failed configuration change after the restart.\\\" % ex)\nlims.append(\\\"The same receipt's declared comparison was recorded as unknown because the prerequisite event is labeled phantom_commit and the result event phantom_restart, so the two were not correlated; the restart finding rests on the recorded events rather than on an evaluated comparison, and later requests for this account should use one case label across the case and result events.\\\")\n\njoint=cur['joint_history']+(\\\" Receipt %s comes from a further experiment identifier, 0846354b7a2c4a19a603cce0eeb6be27-experiment, which keeps the failed configuration write, the partition and the lone commit of the earlier grown-direction cases and adds a restart of the leader over its own stores.\\\" % ex)\n\nk0=kn['6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-knowledge-0']; k1=kn['6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-knowledge-1']\ne0=dict(k0['executions']); e0[ex]=[0]\ne1=dict(k1['executions']); e1[ex]=[0]\n\nupd={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpret receipt %s, the restart probe for the grown direction of the phantom-configuration account. The phantom commit reproduced exactly as in the earlier grown cases, and the restart loaded only the committed pair with the new server absent, so the account keeps its violated conclusion and asserted defect claim while recording that the phantom configuration is process-local and that the entry committed under it stays in the log without a recorded commit index. The update also records that the request's comparison did not correlate because its two events use different case labels.\\\" % ex,\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k0['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k0['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k0['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k0['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e0},\n  {\\\"id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"kind\\\":k1['kind'],\\\"statement\\\":k1['statement'],\\\"conditions\\\":k1['conditions'],\\\"source_ids\\\":k1['source_ids'],\\\"executions\\\":e1},\n ],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"6491640ed49a4c7b8f5150438d350e36-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"0846354b7a2c4a19a603cce0eeb6be27-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":cur['source_ids'],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{ex:[0,1]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":cur['rationale']+\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\"+para,\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":ces,\n  \\\"limitations\\\":lims,\n  \\\"joint_history\\\":joint,\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k0['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k0['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"appendConfigurationEntry installs the new configuration in memory regardless of whether its log entry was stored.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":k1['id'],\\\"revision\\\":k1['revision']+1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"quorumSize, electSelf and setupLeaderState derive voter sets from the latest configuration.\\\"},\n  ],\n }],\n}\njson.dump(upd, open('draft/update.json','w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nopen('draft/update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\nimport json,jsonschema\ns=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json'))\nd=json.load(open('/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-17_17-50-22-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/update.json'))\njsonschema.validate(d,s);i=d['interpretations'][0]\nprint('schema OK', [(u['revision']) for u in i['knowledge']], len(i['counterevidence']), len(i['limitations']))\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
